    schema:datePosted "2026-09-03"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Who We Are: At Bandwidth, we shape how the world connects. We're the global communications software company and Tier 1 network operator with global reach. The voice, messaging, and emergency services infrastructure behind the brands and apps you use every day. Because we own the network we build on, the problems you'll solve here are bigger, more complex, and more impactful. And as communications shifts to AI, we're the infrastructure layer making it possible. We call ourselves BANDmates because building something this big takes collaboration, different perspectives, and the freedom to bring your authentic self to the table. We're experts who speak like humans. Ready to build what's next? #JoinTheBand What We Are Looking For: Bandwidth is building a dedicated Salesforce Alliance team to win the global contact center market. As Director of Salesforce Alliance Pipeline & Development, you will own and grow Bandwidth's relationship with Salesforce — building the contacts, credibility, and pipeline motion that makes Bandwidth the undisputed carrier of choice for Salesforce's Agentforce contact center platform. You will be Bandwidth's face to Salesforce's partner and field teams globally, coordinating inbound and outbound lead flow, aligning go-to-market strategy, and managing two field-based direct reports who work the Salesforce event circuit in Europe and North America. This is a high-visibility, externally-facing role that requires deep knowledge of Salesforce's internal structure, the contact center ecosystem, and carrier-grade voice and messaging. What You'll Do: SALESFORCE RELATIONSHIP OWNERSHIP Build and maintain deep, trusted relationships across Salesforce's partner, alliances, Agentforce, and contact center teams — from individual contributors to executive sponsors Serve as Bandwidth's primary point of contact for Salesforce's ISV/partner and co-sell programs Maintain a comprehensive map of Salesforce contacts relevant to contact center, Agentforce, and the carrier partner ecosystem Facilitate executive engagement between Bandwidth and Salesforce leadership on a regular cadence PIPELINE GENERATION & LEAD FLOW Drive mutual pipeline between Bandwidth and Salesforce — both generating leads from Salesforce and routing Bandwidth-sourced leads into Salesforce deals Build and manage a structured lead-exchange process with Salesforce's alliance and field teams Track and report Salesforce-influenced and co-sell pipeline, maintaining accurate data in CRM Set pipeline generation targets for the team and hold direct reports accountable AGENTFORCE CONTACT CENTER STRATEGY Develop and maintain Bandwidth's value proposition for Salesforce's Agentforce contact center — articulating why Bandwidth is the right carrier partner Understand the competitive landscape in contact center carriers (Twilio, Vonage, NICE, Genesys, Five9, etc.) and keep Salesforce informed of Bandwidth's differentiation Work with Bandwidth product and marketing teams to ensure Salesforce-relevant content, case studies, and technical documentation are current Support Salesforce field teams in positioning Bandwidth on active contact center pursuits TEAM LEADERSHIP Manage and develop two Field Alliance Executives (Europe and North America) Coach direct reports on Salesforce's internal contacts, deal mechanics, and co-sell motion Set quarterly OKRs for the team aligned to Bandwidth's Salesforce partnership goals Represent the team's results to Bandwidth leadership EVENTS & EXECUTIVE PRESENCE Plan and execute Bandwidth's presence at Salesforce events: World Tour London, Dreamforce (San Francisco), World Tour New York, and other regional events Represent Bandwidth at Salesforce partner summits, QBRs, and advisory boards What You Need: 7+ years in partnerships, alliances, or channel sales — ideally in SaaS, UCaaS, CCaaS, or carrier/telecom Direct experience working within or alongside the Salesforce ecosystem (ISV partner, Salesforce employee, or Salesforce-focused sales role) Demonstrable contact network within Salesforce's partner, ISV, or field organization Deep understanding of the contact center market — platforms, carriers, competitive dynamics Experience managing and developing a team Exceptional executive presence and relationship-building skills Based in London or willing to relocate Bonus Points: Experience with Salesforce's AppExchange ISV program or Salesforce Partner Program Familiarity with carrier-grade voice, SIP, or CPaaS Experience at a global communications provider (Twilio, NICE, Genesys, Vonage, 8x8, or similar) Network within the Salesforce Agentforce / Einstein for Service team What Success Looks Like — First 12 Months Deep, active relationships established across Salesforce's partner, Agentforce, and field organization Structured lead-exchange process in place and generating measurable pipeline Both direct reports ramped, active at Salesforce events, and running co-sell motions Bandwidth positioned as the go-to carrier reference for Salesforce contact center deals Active pipeline attributable to the Salesforce alliance visible in CRM The Whole Person Promise: At Bandwidth, we're pretty proud of our corporate culture, which is rooted in our \"Whole Person Promise.\" We promise all employees that they can have meaningful work AND a full life, and we provide a work environment geared toward enriching your body, mind, and spirit. How do we do that? Well… Work laptop & mobile phone with a competitive subscription plan, and an internet allowance to support the costs of the Internet at home. We contribute 8% of your monthly gross salary into your private pension. Income protection plan to ensure you'll receive a regular income if you are unable to work due to illness or injury. Life insurance providing financial support to your loved ones in the event of your unexpected passing. Health insurance, with extensive coverage, a simple claim process and the possibility to cover your life partner and children. Extensive Employee Assistance Programme, offering 24/7 counseling and support on all areas of life (personal and professional). Unlimited, free and anonymous consultations with our dedicated therapist. Childcare support Cycle to work scheme 24 days annual leave per year and 1 additional day every 3 years. Time-Off Embargo. When you take time off (of any kind!) you're embargoed from working. Bandmates and managers are not allowed to interrupt your time-off - not even with email. Additional time-off can be earned throughout the year through volunteer hours and Bandwidth challenges. \"Mahalo moments\" program grants additional time off for life's most important moments like graduations, buying a first home, getting married, wedding anniversaries (every five years), and the birth of a grandchild. 90-Minute Workout Lunches, contribution to your monthly fitness subscription and unlimited virtual meetings with our very own nutritionist. Are you excited about the position and its responsibilities, but not sure if you're 100% qualified? Do you feel you can work to help us crush the mission? If you answered 'yes' to both of these questions, we encourage you to apply! You won't want to miss the opportunity to be a part of the BAND. Applicant Privacy Notice Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
