    schema:datePosted "2026-09-04"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Your mission You design & code data transformations, pipelines & dashboards to implement different business use cases on our data platform (Databricks/Spark, Python, SQL, Power BI) You assist in integrating APIs and third-party services into existing systems. Debugging and troubleshooting to ensure seamless data flow and functionality You will be proficient in utilizing GIT in Azure DevOps for collaborative programming environments, including code repository management, branching, merging, resolving conflicts, pull requests, code reviews, and CI/CD pipeline integration You will help in the operation and maintenance of our billing engine workflows used for invoicing our b2b customers (Python (Spark, Pandas), Databricks, Azure Functions). Assist in the creation and maintenance of AI-driven dashboards in Databricks. Your profile You are an enrolled student (preferably with a technical degree) with previous experience in coding, preferably Python with libraries like pandas, numpy, spark, SQL or/and Power BI and 1-2 years of study ahead of you Your mindset is to complete tasks consciously, reliably, and end-to-end, with a high level of personal commitment You possess a strong attention to detail, consistently ensuring the precision and accuracy of all shared data within the team You have a hands-on mentality, pick up what needs to be done to complete your project You are business fluent in English, German is a good addition, but not a must Optional: experience with cloud services like AWS, GCP preferably Azure (e.g. Azure Databricks, Azure Data Factory) Why us? People take centre stage: Become part of a dynamic, ambitious and agile team that develops solutions for the eMobility market and be part of our EDRI events or the next after-work event With us, you get the best of both worlds - 100% start-up with the support of a large company The freedom you need: We offer you hybrid working with flexible working hours Competitive compensation and up to 30 days of vacation per year, depending on your weekly working hours You get everything you need to get started: onboarding with welcome gifts and all the hardware you need A unique work environment in the heart of Essen – with free drinks, snacks, and our very own coffee station Contact Diversity counts at E.ON. We welcome all people and are convinced that differences make us stronger. Become part of our inclusive and diverse corporate culture! Seize the opportunity to become part of our E.ON Drive Infrastructure team and not only create prospects for the future of E.ON, but also for your own. We look forward to getting to know you! Sharin Working Student Do you have any questions or difficulties with your application? Please contact me at ----- Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
