    schema:description "Your mission Conduct market, industry, and competitor research to identify relevant trends and strategic opportunities Screen studies, reports, and market analyses and translate findings into actionable insights Monitor and analyze market and business KPIs to support strategic decision-making Support the development of a platform-based approach for organizing and sharing market intelligence Create compelling PowerPoint presentations and prepare reports tailored to different stakeholder groups Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders and proactively contribute ideas to improve processes and ways of working Your profile Currently enrolled in a bachelor's or master's program in International Management, Business Administration, Economics, or a related field First experience in market research, strategy, consulting, the eMobility industry, or AI agent development is a plus Strong analytical skills, a high affinity for numbers, and an interest in market developments and business insights Highly organized, proactive, and comfortable working in a dynamic environment Strong communication skills with the ability to adapt messages to different stakeholder groups Proficiency in PowerPoint, with the ability to structure information and create compelling presentations Strong Excel skills and confidence in working with data and KPIs Fluent in German and English Why us? People take centre stage: Become part of a dynamic, ambitious and agile team that develops solutions for the eMobility market and be part of our EDRI events or the next after-work event With us, you get the best of both worlds - 100% start-up with the support of a large company The freedom you need: We offer you hybrid working with flexible working hours Competitive compensation and up to 30 days of vacation per year, depending on your weekly working hours You get everything you need to get started: onboarding with welcome gifts and all the hardware you need A unique work environment in the heart of Essen – with free drinks, snacks, and our very own coffee station Contact Diversity counts at E.ON. We welcome all people and are convinced that differences make us stronger. Become part of our inclusive and diverse corporate culture! Seize the opportunity to become part of our E.ON Drive Infrastructure team and not only create prospects for the future of E.ON, but also for your own. We look forward to getting to know you! Sharin Working Student Do you have any questions or difficulties with your application? Please contact me at ----- Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
